  "description": "Reid Tanami eBike | Electric gravel bike\nReady for the road less travelled – an electric gravel bike combining smooth pedal assistance, versatile gearing and a lightweight alloy frame for exploring further.\nThe Reid Tanami eBike brings together the versatility of a gravel bike with the added support of electric assistance, making it a great choice for longer rides, mixed-surface routes and everyday adventures.\nIts 6061 alloy frame features internal cable routing and a fully integrated 36V 352Wh battery for a clean, streamlined design. A flat chainstay yoke helps create a shorter rear end, while the rigid 700c alloy fork with 12mm thru-axle provides responsive handling and stability across different surfaces. Available in four frame sizes, the Tanami offers options to suit a range of riders.\nAn Ananda R400 250W rear hub motor delivers smooth, responsive electric assistance to support your pedalling on longer rides and challenging routes. The integrated Ananda DF26 display features Bluetooth connectivity through the Ananda app, allowing riders to monitor essential ride information and battery status. With an approximate range of up to 30 miles (48km), depending on terrain and riding style, the 352Wh battery provides support for a variety of journeys.\nA Microshift Advent 9-speed drivetrain offers a versatile range of gearing, with an 11-46T cassette to help tackle changing gradients and varied terrain. Tektro C550 mechanical disc brakes provide controlled stopping power, while Kenda K1185 700 x 50c tyres offer grip, stability and comfort across gravel paths, country lanes and tarmac.\nCompleting the setup are 700c WTB double-wall rims, compact alloy handlebars and comfortable bar tape, alongside a WTB Rocket saddle for support on longer rides. With its practical gravel geometry, electric assistance and versatile components, the Tanami is built for riders looking to explore beyond their usual routes.\nThe Tanami eBike is ideal for:\n\nGravel riding and exploration, with a versatile setup for mixed-surface routes and off-road paths\n\nLonger rides and adventures, supported by a 250W Ananda rear hub motor and integrated 352Wh battery\n\nCountry lanes and everyday road riding, with responsive handling and comfortable 700 x 50c tyres\n\nRiders tackling varied terrain, with a Microshift Advent 9-speed drivetrain and wide-range 11-46T cassette\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with compact handlebars, comfortable bar tape and a WTB Rocket saddle\n\nRiders looking for dependable stopping power, with Tektro mechanical disc brakes\n\nCyclists wanting a streamlined electric gravel bike, with an integrated battery and internal cable routing\n\nRiders looking for the right frame fit, with four available sizes from 48cm to 57cm\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
